      {
        "id": "one-kind-many-makers",
        "kind": "try",
        "blocks": [],
        "lead": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "In 1967 Hilary Putnam argued that pain might occur in humans, in an octopus with a very different nervous system and, in principle, in silicon. If pain were one particular brain state, creatures without it could not feel pain."
          }
        ],
        "reveal": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "That is multiple realisability: the same table can be implemented by gears, neurons or chips, so the same mental kind can have many physical realisers."
          }
        ],
